  "engineeringConclusion": "New lower API 0.2 integration collides with faithfully retained later nightly 0.1 adapters. Nightly dependency constraints were internally aligned. a23 adapts local client and pins but lacks the later source reviewer in both d797 and a23; absence is an older-baseline omission, not proof of an a23 deletion. Pin changes alone cannot restore imports/evidence semantics.",
  "serverConclusion": "The uncommitted a23 __main__ replacement removes the preserved nightly HTTP launch protocol. Keeping HTTP launch and separate one-shot ordessa CLI is possible; the original HTTP main cannot be restored verbatim because its composition calls UnitRuntimeOwner and the old product plan/build_runtime seam. Current RegistryRuntime has no lifecycle, /live, token/bootstrap or listening announcement. Needs host-only composition/lifecycle adaptation over current capabilities, not rollback to Unit."
